      "heading": "Students Still Run Into Trouble",
      "content": {
        "kind": "bundle",
        "sourceNeedCount": 2,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "needId": "checklist:3",
            "type": "checklist",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Subject combination: medical courses, for example, need Physics, Chemistry, Biology or Biotechnology and English, as the NIOS FAQ points out."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Part admission: a learner who takes up to four subjects while holding another board's certificate gets only a marksheet, not a certificate."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Age and attempts: the FAQ gives minimum ages (14 for Secondary, 15 as on 31 July for Senior Secondary) and says admission is valid for five years."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "A single notice: a job or a course can name the boards it accepts, so read its qualification line."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Document mismatch: names, dates of birth and enrolment details must match your other records."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "where-trouble",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 3
          },
          {
            "needId": "checklist:6",
            "type": "checklist",
            "heading": "Skills Beside the Certificate: Free Routes First",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "YouTube lessons and free public courses on SWAYAM for spreadsheets, spoken English, design or beginner coding."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "NIOS also lists vocational courses, so check the current list on its site and ask about recognition before enrolling."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Library books and a real task you can watch someone do."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Local internships, shop work or family business tasks where you can show output."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "learn",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 6
          }
        ]
      },
      "type": "checklist",
      "title": "Students Still Run Into Trouble"
